# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# TOON Linode devnet — nginx reverse proxy (template).
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# `${DOMAIN}` is the ONLY placeholder; bootstrap.sh renders this to
# nginx/conf.d/devnet.conf with:  envsubst '${DOMAIN}' < template > conf.d/devnet.conf
# (the single-var filter leaves nginx's own $host/$http_upgrade/... untouched).
#
# Backends are referenced through the `$backend` variable + the Docker embedded
# resolver (127.0.0.11) so nginx boots even if a chain container is briefly down
# or still starting (lazy, per-request resolution instead of boot-time).
#
# NOTHING RUNS THIS FILE TODAY. The self-hosted chain box was deleted 2026-07-19
# (see ../README.md's banner and ../endpoints.json) and the devnet settles on
# public chains; `*.devnet.toonprotocol.dev` is a wildcard A record to the
# registrar's parking host, so `mina.` and `evm-rpc.` answer a 301 to
# toonprotocol.dev and fail TLS. The file is committed because
# `.github/workflows/devnet-deploy.yml` still renders it via bootstrap.sh (last
# run 2026-06-23) — treat it as the artifact a rebuilt chain box would start
# from, not as a description of anything currently serving traffic.

# Per-IP rate limits for the public RPC/faucet endpoints (devnet abuse guard).
limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=rpc:10m rate=30r/s;

# WebSocket upgrade plumbing (used by the Solana WS endpoint; harmless elsewhere).
map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {
    default upgrade;
    ''      close;
}

# Subdomain -> chain backend (Docker service name + port on the shared network).
# Chains-only: the connector/relay app edge deploys separately (deploy/relay-edge +
# deploy/pay-edge) and is NOT fronted here.
map $host $backend {
    default               "";
    evm-rpc.${DOMAIN}     "http://anvil:8545";
    solana-rpc.${DOMAIN}  "http://solana-validator:8899";
    solana-ws.${DOMAIN}   "http://solana-validator:8900";
    faucet.${DOMAIN}      "http://faucet:3500";
}

# ── Port 80: ACME challenge + redirect everything else to HTTPS ──────────────
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name evm-rpc.${DOMAIN} solana-rpc.${DOMAIN} solana-ws.${DOMAIN}
                faucet.${DOMAIN} mina.${DOMAIN};

    location /.well-known/acme-challenge/ {
        root /var/www/certbot;
    }
    location / {
        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
    }
}

# ── Port 443: chain RPC / WS / faucet (one block, host-routed) ───────────────
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    listen [::]:443 ssl;
    http2 on;
    server_name evm-rpc.${DOMAIN} solana-rpc.${DOMAIN} solana-ws.${DOMAIN} faucet.${DOMAIN};

    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/evm-rpc.${DOMAIN}/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/evm-rpc.${DOMAIN}/privkey.pem;
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

    resolver 127.0.0.11 valid=10s ipv6=off;

    location / {
        if ($backend = "") { return 404; }       # unknown subdomain
        limit_req zone=rpc burst=60 nodelay;

        proxy_pass $backend;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;

        # WebSocket upgrade (Solana WS subscriptions on solana-ws.*).
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;
        proxy_read_timeout 1h;

        client_max_body_size 4m;                  # JSON-RPC batch ceiling
    }
}

# ── Port 443: Mina — passthrough to the PUBLIC devnet (no local node) ────────
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    listen [::]:443 ssl;
    http2 on;
    server_name mina.${DOMAIN};

    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/evm-rpc.${DOMAIN}/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/evm-rpc.${DOMAIN}/privkey.pem;
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

    resolver 1.1.1.1 8.8.8.8 valid=300s;

    # THE URI PART BELOW IS DELIBERATE AND IT WORKS. It is the one `proxy_pass`
    # in this repo that carries a URI on a variable upstream, so it looks like
    # the defect issue #987 describes. It is not, and #987's rule is wrong:
    # nginx does NOT ignore a URI part on a variable `proxy_pass`. Its own docs
    # say the opposite — "if URI is specified in the directive, it is passed to
    # the server as is, replacing the original request URI" — and issue #1023
    # measured it on nginx 1.18 through 1.31 and end-to-end against the real
    # upstream: this block, run verbatim, returns 200 from api.minascan.io,
    # while the shape #987 predicts (`proxy_pass $mina_upstream$request_uri;`)
    # returns 404, because minascan serves /node/devnet/v1/graphql and 404s
    # /graphql. So the two readings are distinguishable and this is the working
    # one. See `no_variable_upstream_carries_a_static_uri_part` in
    # crates/connector-bin/tests/devnet_configs_load.rs, which exempts exactly
    # this line and carries the whole argument.
    #
    # What IS true of a URI part on a variable upstream: it is STATIC. It
    # replaces the entire request URI, so neither the path past `location
    # /graphql` nor the query string reaches the upstream. Both are wanted here
    # — minascan serves this API at one fixed path, the GraphQL request travels
    # in the POST body, and forwarding args to that upstream measurably raised
    # its error rate (#1023). Anywhere the remainder or the args must survive,
    # use this box's other form instead: `rewrite ^.*$ /<target> break;` and a
    # `proxy_pass` naming host and port only.
    location /graphql {
        limit_req zone=rpc burst=60 nodelay;
        set $mina_upstream "https://api.minascan.io";
        proxy_pass $mina_upstream/node/devnet/v1/graphql;
        proxy_ssl_server_name on;
        proxy_set_header Host api.minascan.io;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }
    location / { return 404; }                     # only proxy /graphql
}
